Description: CVE-2025-71330 - ICNS zero-length entry denial of service (CWE-835)
 A crafted ICNS buffer whose entry-length field is zero never advances the
 parser offset, so calculate() loops forever and blocks the Node.js event loop.
 .
 Rewritten as a leftover patch: in 2.0.2 this is the same non-advancing-offset
 defect as CVE-2025-71329. The compiled dist/ guards (entryLength < 8 and
 findBox forward progress) are already applied by patches/CVE-2025-71329.
 Re-applying the upstream ICNS/HEIF/JXL hunks here is redundant and causes
 "Reversed (or previously applied) patch detected" failures during the build.
 This file keeps a dedicated regression test only.
 .
 Verified against the 2.0.2 npm tarball: unpatched, the ICNS fixture hangs;
 with CVE-2025-71329 applied, the assertion passes.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/image-size/image-size/pull/439
Last-Update: 2026-09-29

--- /dev/null
